  "warnings": [
    "ESP32-S3 internal SRAM has 32 KiB of instruction/cache storage, 416 KiB shared by instruction and data addresses, and 64 KiB of data/cache storage. The overlapping IRAM and DRAM windows map one 512 KiB resource and are counted once.",
    "Full SRAM capacity includes cache, ROM/bootloader, and other reservations. It is not the available heap; only captured allocator free chunks establish free bytes.",
    "The 32 MiB external data and instruction windows are address apertures, not installed flash or PSRAM capacity. Flash and PSRAM can share the data aperture; no linear physical mapping or duplicate storage is inferred.",
    "Configured flash and PSRAM capacities are added only from matching effective build configuration. They remain unmapped and unobserved: runtime probing, MMU page tables, image headers and partition offsets are not supplied by this descriptor.",
    "RTC fast RAM has one shared instruction/data address window and is counted once. RTC slow RAM can reserve space for the ULP; ownership and deep-sleep retention are not observed.",
    "CoreS3 and ESP32-S3 DevKit use this common SoC layout. CoreS3 BSP registration comes from the retained NXRS patch listed in upstream/memory-layouts/sources.json. Neither a board name nor an ELF alone attests a connected physical device."
  ],
